--TEST--
What a matched route says about which route it is comes from the unit and its captures are the peer's, so only the captures refuse a plain `string` — `rule:routing/matched-once-before-the-handler`, `rule:security/tainted-qualifier`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Agreement, asked of the two things one `Core\Router\Match` carries: what
// decides the qualifier is where the value came from, and nothing about which
// member answered it. `is` compares the match with a method reference the unit
// wrote, so its `bool` is the unit's own and the first binding below compiles;
// a capture is a segment of the path the request arrived with, so a plain
// `string` target refuses it and the last binding does not compile.
//
// Both halves are load-bearing. A match whose identity were tainted would make
// a route unusable at every branch that picks a handler, and one that marked
// neither would launder the request path through the route table, which is the
// direction that costs.
class Posts {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/posts/{id}", method: Core\Http\Method::Get)]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public static function show(uint $id): string { return "post"; }
}

var $matched = Core\Request::route();
if ($matched != null) {
    bool $isShow = $matched->is(Posts::show);
    foreach ($matched->params() as mixed $each) {
    }
    string $segment = $matched->param("id") ?? "0";
}
// covers: Core\Router\Match::is, Core\Router\Match::params, Core\Router\Match::param
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `string|uint|int|decimal|tainted string|Core\Uuid|Parses`
   --> case.nvs:24:23
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
